    "reading": "ECO-1 item 1 requires TPS72325 pin3 (EN) to move from GND to V_NLDO_IN; it currently reads 'GND', so the fatal B1 condition is still on this board. PROJECT_STATUS records AVDD=21 before ECO-1 and 20 after, and this board has 21. Both say the same thing: the schematic-side ECO-1 was never pushed into the PCB (Import Changes was not run), so the KiCad board S3 receives is the PRE-ECO layout and must take ECO-1 as well as L1-L6.",
    "caveat": "Pin functions (RESV1, GPIO1-4, VCAP2/3) cannot be read off the PCB -- only pad numbers exist there. The unconnected ADS1299 pads are listed above; map them to pin names via the schematic symbol before acting."
